- **`MyClass`**: This is the name of the class you want to create.
- **`myMethod`**: This is the method within the class that will be called.

### Example:
```csharp
public class MyClass
{
    public void myMethod()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        // 1. Create a new instance of the class.
        var instance = new MyClass();

        // 2. Call the method on the instance.
        instance.myMethod();
    }
}
```

In this example, `MyClass` contains a single method `myMethod`, which prints "Hello, World!" when called. The `Program` class demonstrates how to create an instance of `MyClass` and call its method.

